# Validation pipeline

Before any drawing leaves the office it must pass these checks **in the
order shown**. Stop at the first failure and report.

## Stage 1 — Quick layout sanity

When the layout is still a JSON / structured object (before drawing):

```
validate_layout_quick(layout)
```

Fails on:
- room area below СНиП minimum (rule `09-snip-neufert.mdc`)
- door / window widths not in the standard schedule (rule `02-units-dims.mdc`, `05-typology-bina.mdc`)
- circulation < 900 mm

## Stage 2 — Drawing structural validation

After geometry is created in modelspace:

```
validate_drawing
```

Fails on:
- standard 11 layer set absent (rule `02-units-dims.mdc`)
- duplicated geometry (lines on top of lines)
- text not on `TEXT` layer / dim not on `DIM` layer
- MText not using `\fSylfaen` override (rule `00-georgian-text.mdc`)
- title block missing (rule `01-title-block.mdc`)

## Stage 3 — Metrics

```
compute_metrics(contextJsonPath)
```

Reports:
- room count, area totals
- glazing ratio per room (must be ≥ 1/8)
- circulation ratio (corridor m² / total m²)
- furniture coverage per room

## Stage 4 — Per-typology check (`scripts/validators/`)

```
(load "scripts/validators/check-min-rooms.lsp")        ; СНиП minima
(load "scripts/validators/check-title-block.lsp")      ; title block presence
```

## Stage 5 — GRG cross-check (when applicable)

```
(load "scripts/utilities/compute-grg-k.lsp")
```

Returns K1, K2, K2-1 (FAR), K3 and compares against the FZ thresholds in
rule `06-grg-coefficients.mdc`.

## Stage 6 — Visual self-check

```
(command "_.ZOOM" "_E")
(command "_.REGENALL")
```

Then export a screenshot via the MCP `export_to_image` tool and inspect
manually.

## Stage 7 — Issue

Only after stages 1 – 6 pass:

```
(command "_.QSAVE")
;; export PDF / DXF as needed:
batch_export(format = "pdf", out_folder = "...")
```

## Failure-report format

When a check fails, return a JSON like:

```
{
  "stage": "Stage 2",
  "rule": "02-units-dims.mdc",
  "check": "standard layer set",
  "missing": ["WALL", "DOOR", "WINDOW"],
  "found":   ["A-Wall", "kar-panjara_*", "Doors_*"],
  "fix":     "run scripts/utilities/layer-remap-to-standard.lsp"
}
```

Always include the **rule reference** + the **fix command** in every
failure entry.

## When to skip stages

- Conceptual sketches: only Stage 1.
- Quick re-do of an existing sheet: Stage 2 + 3 + 6.
- Final issue / handover: every stage, no skips.
